this past week ubisoft were kind enough  to let us try out  siege's newest seasonal update now  there's a lot to talk about a favela  rework  a three-speed healer on defense and  numerous nips and tucks to things like  barrel attachments  bullet holes and oh baby the bearing  nine  here is everything you need to know  about north  star  okay so before we dive into things you  know the drill  like the video subscribe to the channel  and turn on notifications  because hey you like siege i like siege  let's talk about siege okay so first  things first  the new operator thunderbird she is a  three-speed  one armor defender whose primary gadget  called a kona  is literally an automated turret that  shoots out  darkstims it operates on a cool down and  like doc's stim heals or overheals  anyone who ventures into its area of  effect  this includes attackers it's also worth  mentioning that anyone who is in a down  but not out state  can crawl over to a kona it shoots a  stim into you and  voila you're resurrected so how do you  use it  well as far as walkthroughs go it's  pretty easy you put it on the ground  wait for it to charge up and watch as it  heals your homies  she gets three of them meaning that she  can pop say one on each site and since  she is a three speed with a frag heavy  loadout  take one with her as she roams off sight  to hold a choke  which brings us to thunderbirds kit now  in terms of primary they gave her  finca's assault rifle the spear 308  making her the only defender aside from  wamai  to carry an ar they also gave her cavs  auto shoddy which could actually be sick  considering that she gets the much  improved bearing 9 as her secondary  which we'll touch upon when we talk  about barrel attachments  she also gets legion and ying's pistol  but  who cares for her secondary gadget you  get to choose between a nitro cell  or impact needless to say it's likely  that she'll be played as a kind of  jaeger-esque put it down and forget  about it type roamer  it's also likely that because of that  she'll be  pretty popular and ranked the point is  obviously to go  kind of nuts with her since she outputs  healing whether or not she's alive  so naturally i gave her to our new 18  year old video editor told him to crush  a g-fuel and said  hey eat up kid  okay chill that said thunderbirds kit is  very versatile and i could actually see  a universe in which  on certain sites you could run her as an  anchor  think about it you've got spammable self  healing an auto shoddy  a nitro cell and a truly excellent  smg which segues us perfectly into the  next subject of interest  barrel attachment changes in short  ubisoft have both  reworked and simplified barrel  attachments such that they actually  well make sense in addition to you know  hiding flash  the flash hider is now strictly  responsible for dampening vertical  recoil  the compensator continues to mitigate  recoil from left to right  and the muzzle break helps recenter a  weapon more quickly whilst one tapping  the suppressor remains  entirely useless which makes me really  sad because i was really hoping they  would do something with that  anyway this obviously impacts certain  weapons more than others  most of the already easy to use guns  felt pretty much the same  i didn't notice much of a difference  with ying's lmg or  sledge's ar for instance since they  already boast a relatively low rate of  fire  twitch drones after uh  crazy that said there were some  notoriously unwieldy weapons for which  it seemed to make a  huge difference such as the f2 now don't  get me wrong this does not hold a candle  to the  old pre-nerf muzzle plus acog f2  because that thing was but this new one  with flash hider  not too shabby dude this thing is so  hard to control  yes  but where the barrel attachments became  most noticeable for me at least  was on one particular machine pistol the  bearing 9  whose recoil has been foobard for quite  some time  now i'm not sure if it's just because of  the attachments or if uv rebalanced  machine pistols specifically  but man does this thing go burr that  said there did  also seem to be some recoil nerfs the  most noticeable of which  was ash running either flash or  comp her r4c felt unexpectedly  unwieldy and by unwieldy i mean  unwieldy like we're talking something  along the lines of the recent jaeger  nerf where even with the hollow  the kick was just incredibly noticeable  they also  took away that third ash charge that  they just gave her  so rip ash i guess  next the map rework favela honestly when  it comes to siege maps  it's kind of just impossible to make  real  substantial pronouncements this early is  it better than it was  [ __ ] absolutely is it good  who knows the biggest difference is that  they removed a ton  of the external walls making the map  much  closer to being well you know playable  it's still pretty clowny though that  said it continues to be hard as [ __ ] to  see  anyone on the damn thing and it still  feels as if there's tons of  weird tight claustrophobic choke points  plus i don't know about you but  i still can't load into this map and not  play like an  absolute idiot  the next big change is the stuff that  happens post-death  one absolutely massive quality of life  upgrade is that ubisoft  finally took out client-sided bodies and  implemented a kind of  translucent valerant-esque operator icon  in their stead  this means that when you die your body  just fades away  instead of becoming a highly annoying  meat shield they've also  re-jigged the post-death sequence  somewhat making it a little more  apparent to new players how it is they  got fragged  and what will happen in the seconds  following the kill itself  next are some very big changes to the  support mode that were unveiled earlier  this year  namely being able to use drones and  cameras  after death now to be clear this is only  coming to the test server  not the live build so before you start  screaming at devs on twitter about how  the game is dead  please register the fact that this is  only being  tested not implemented  tested so yes you heard me you can now  hop on  any previously deployed drones after  death and drive them around as if you  were alive  yokais twitches mozzies you name it  you can also hop on cameras which  includes maestros  bulletproofs etc speaking of  bulletproofs they're now able to be  rotated and have been equipped with an  emp shock that can be discharged  by yes dead defenders in terms of other  small but  significant quality of life changes they  got rid of bullet holes  meaning that you can no longer clap  someone through an imperceptible hole  that you made earlier in the round  i think i speak for everybody when i say  thank [ __ ]  god they also made it so that melusi's  gadgets are no longer bulletproof  this one's pretty straightforward and  let's be honest  long overdue yubi also finally got  around to fixing the game's  smoke propagation system so for  technical reasons that are way above  my head and i have no hope of  understanding toxic babes can no longer  clip through walls and deny  plants in the dumbest ways imaginable  last but not least and this one's really  interesting  they've made it so that you can melee  mira windows  maestro cams and bulletproof cams and  render the actual glass  impossible to see through needless to  say  this is going to make these things way  less oppressive the cams are still  usable  mind you like maestro can still open his  camera and go pew pew  but he now has to be super careful when  denying plants or hard breeches  playing strictly off of intel and sound  cues  so on the whole a pretty great update  not game changing by any means but  great aside from the fact that i'd wish  they'd just gone ahead and added player  outlines  if cs go can copy it from valoran so can  you ubisoft  i think that northstar is a step in the  right direction and i for one  can't wait to see where they go from  here  inside you can go for it  come on get him for the views man he's  right there  oh my god
 

